🎭 SECTION 1: THE ARCHETYPES (Who they are)
Backstabber: A partner (or friend) who pretends to be loyal while actively working against your interests or reputation behind your back.
Catfish: Someone who creates a completely false online identity (using fake photos and stories) to lure people into emotional or financial traps.
Con-Artist (Romantic): A professional manipulator who uses "Love" as a tool to gain access to a woman’s money, credit, home, or status.
Femme Fatale: A seductive woman whose charm leads men into compromising or dangerous situations.
Golden Goose: Also known as the "Benefactor" or "The Trick." This is the person who provides all the financial resources in a lopsided relationship. The "Golden Goose" is often being "mined" rather than loved.
High-Value Man/Woman: A person who possesses integrity, emotional intelligence, financial stability, and a strong personal philosophy. They don't just have assets; they have character.
Minion: A weak-willed person who follows the lead of a more dominant manipulator, often helping them carry out games or spying.
Playette / Playgirl: The female version of a player. She uses her sex appeal and "Vixen" energy to juggle multiple men for attention or resources.
Player: A person who treats relationships as a game of conquest. A "True Player" knows the rules of social interaction, but a "Low-Level Player" is simply a sex addict with a script.
Ride-or-Die: A term for extreme loyalty. While often seen as a goal, NOLA warns that "Ride-or-Die" can become a trap where a woman stays with a man who is "driving them both off a cliff."
Side-Piece / Sidekick: The person kept in the background of a main relationship. They are the "Back-up Plan" used for sex or ego-boosting when the main partner is unavailable.
Siren: An archetype of a woman whose voice and beauty are used to distract a man from his goals or common sense.
Vixen: A woman who is highly aware of her sex appeal and uses it aggressively to navigate social and romantic circles.
Waffler: The "Wishy-Washy" man or woman. They cannot make a decision, they avoid labels, and they often allow their mothers or ex-partners to dictate their current life.
Whole Package, The: A person who has it all: looks, brains, bank account, and a good heart. (NOLA: "Very rare, sis. Check the receipts first.")

🎲 SECTION 2: RELATIONSHIP GAMES & TACTICS
Abandonment: The act of leaving a partner without warning or emotional support, often used by Wafflers when things get "too real."
Breadcrumbing: Giving just enough attention (a text every few days, a like on a photo) to keep a person interested without ever intending to commit.
Deception: The intentional hiding of the truth regarding one's past, current relationship status, or intentions.
Future-Faking: Painting a vivid picture of a future together (marriage, travel, kids) to keep the partner compliant and invested in the present, with no plan to follow through.
Ghosting: Cutting off all communication without explanation. It is the coward’s exit.
Intermittent Reinforcement: A manipulation tactic where the partner is "perfect" one day and "cruel" the next. This creates an addiction-like bond in the victim.
Kick to the Curb: A swift and final breakup. Usually happens when a Player is finished "Resource Mining" or when a High-Value Woman realizes she’s being played.
Love Bombing: An explosion of affection, gifts, and "Soulmate" talk in the first few weeks designed to bypass a woman’s instincts.
Love Spell: A metaphorical term for being so infatuated that your logic is turned off. (Also refers to the "Woo-woo" techniques some use to try and force love).
One-Night Stand: A single sexual encounter with no intention of a follow-up. Players often mask these as "The start of something special."
Orbiting: When a person who ghosted you continues to "watch" your life by viewing every social media story or liking old posts.
Resource Mining: Using a partner for their car, their Netflix password, their home, or their professional connections.
Triangulation: Bringing a third person (real or imaginary) into the relationship to create jealousy or competition.
Zombieing: When a person who ghosted you suddenly "rises from the dead" and texts you months later as if nothing happened.

