🏛️ SECTION 17: LEGAL & MARRIAGE PROTOCOLS
Alienation of Affection: A legal concept where a third party (a Side-piece or Meddling In-law) is blamed for destroying a marriage.
Alimony (Spousal Support): Financial support paid to a former spouse. (NOLA: "Know if he’s paying it, because that’s money that isn't coming to your household.")
Cohabitation Agreement: A legal contract for unmarried couples living together that defines who owns what and how assets are split if they "Kick to the Curb."
Common Law Marriage: A legal status in some states where a couple is considered married because they lived together for a "Several" years and presented as a couple.
Community Property: Laws stating that anything earned or bought during a marriage belongs 50/50 to both partners.
Domestic Partnership: A legal relationship that provides some, but not all, of the protections of marriage.
Fiduciary Duty: The legal and moral obligation to act in the best interest of the partner (especially regarding shared money).
No-Fault Divorce: A legal exit where neither person has to prove "Cheating" or "Abuse" to end the marriage.
Power of Attorney: Giving a partner the legal right to make medical or financial decisions for you. (NOLA: "Never give this to a Waffler.")
Pre-Nuptial Agreement: A contract signed before marriage to protect individual assets. (NOLA: "A High-Value Woman protects her 'Freedom Fund' before the wedding.")
Separation of Assets: Keeping your bank accounts and property in your own name to avoid "Resource Mining."
Survivor Benefits: Social security or pension money you receive if a spouse passes away.

